    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "As the negative impacts of climate change become increasingly evident, it is paramount to develop\r\ngreen alternatives to existing fuel sources. Hydrogen is a promising replacement to diesel fuel,\r\nand our partner company, Verne Inc., aims to use hydrogen as a fuel source for freight trucks.\r\nWith funding support from Stanford’s Precourt Institute, our team was tasked with designing a\r\nrack that holds Verne’s fuel tanks. The rack will be mounted behind the truck in the ’back-of-cab’\r\narea. Our chosen solution is a rack that holds a maximum of five tanks, utilizing a stacked and\r\nstaggered design to optimize the available space. Additionally, a built-in clamping mechanism\r\nensures that the tanks stay secure during various road conditions. These conditions are defined\r\nas non-crash scenarios, such as vibration from rough surfaces or a sudden shock when hitting\r\npotholes and curbs. Through a series of engineering calculations, shaker table experiments, stress\r\nsimulations, and down-scaled prototypes, we verified our rack’s structural integrity and ease of\r\nassembly. Ultimately, the design meets our customer’s requirements while also having significant\r\nweight and size advantages over other options.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Hong, I., Guerrero, S., Brown, L., and McFarlane, C. (2022). Final Report for a Back-of-Cab Hydrogen Tank Storage Rack. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/gr141yz4859",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
